-- coa13-ch1-shares.l4: the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 17 Chapter 1 (ss 540 to 548): shares and share
-- capital of a company. Lines 7556-7604 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law, objectively, written from the text alone.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the official
-- text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; the rulings of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05
-- refine it). A decision function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN:
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words ("means", "are to", "if", "so long as", "except", a flat negative).
--               Each such branch carries `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<the quoted words>"`.
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide: it lists without closing, says "includes", is silent, leaves a term undefined,
--               points outside the sources, or limits a grant or prohibition in its own wording. Each such branch carries
--               `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`. A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- A definition that yields a sum ("means so much of its share capital as ...") answers a NUMBER.
-- Money is NUMBER in pounds sterling. Every name here begins with the section label it implements.

