`s 543(1) the share must be distinguished by its appropriate number` MEANS
    IF `the company has power under its constitution to issue shares`
    THEN CONSIDER `s 543(2) the share need not have a distinguishing number`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except in the following circumstances" (the exception is met)
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the exception's answer is not known
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Each share in a company having a share capital"

