§§ `Share capital (ss 547 and 548)`

-- ---- s 547: Called-up share capital ----------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7598 | In the Companies Acts—
-- src:7599 | “called-up share capital”, in relation to a company, means so much of its share capital as equals the aggregate amount of the calls made on its shares (whether or not those calls have been paid), together with—
-- src:7600 | (a) any share capital paid up without being called, and
-- src:7601 | (b) any share capital to be paid on a specified future date under the articles, the terms of allotment of the relevant shares or any other arrangements for payment of those shares; and
@ref s 547 "called-up share capital" (src:7598-7601)
GIVEN `the aggregate amount of the calls made on the company's shares, whether or not those calls have been paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the share capital paid up without being called` IS A NUMBER
      `the share capital to be paid on a specified future date under the articles, the terms of allotment or any other arrangements for payment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 547 the company's called-up share capital` MEANS
      `the aggregate amount of the calls made on the company's shares, whether or not those calls have been paid`
    PLUS `the share capital paid up without being called`
    PLUS `the share capital to be paid on a specified future date under the articles, the terms of allotment or any other arrangements for payment`

-- src:7602 | “uncalled share capital” is to be construed accordingly.
@ref s 547 "uncalled share capital" is to be construed accordingly (src:7602)
GIVEN `the company's share capital` IS A NUMBER
      `the company's called-up share capital` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 547 the company's uncalled share capital` MEANS
    -- "construed accordingly": the part of the share capital that is not called up (fork F-547)
    `the company's share capital` MINUS `the company's called-up share capital`

-- ---- s 548: Equity share capital -------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7604 | In the Companies Acts“equity share capital”, in relation to a company, means its issued share capital excluding any part of that capital that, neither as respects dividends nor as respects capital, carries any right to participate beyond a specified amount in a distribution.
@ref s 548 "equity share capital" (src:7604)
GIVEN `the company's issued share capital` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of the issued share capital that neither as respects dividends nor as respects capital carries any right to participate beyond a specified amount in a distribution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 548 the company's equity share capital` MEANS
    `the company's issued share capital`
    MINUS `the part of the issued share capital that neither as respects dividends nor as respects capital carries any right to participate beyond a specified amount in a distribution`

@ref s 548 "equity share capital": which issued shares are within it (src:7604)
GIVEN `the shares are part of the company's issued share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares carry a right to participate beyond a specified amount in a distribution of dividends` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares carry a right to participate beyond a specified amount in a distribution of capital` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 548 the shares are equity share capital` MEANS
    IF     `the shares are part of the company's issued share capital`
       AND (    `the shares carry a right to participate beyond a specified amount in a distribution of dividends`
             OR `the shares carry a right to participate beyond a specified amount in a distribution of capital`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“equity share capital” ... means its issued share capital excluding any part of that capital that, neither as respects dividends nor as respects capital, carries any right to participate beyond a specified amount in a distribution"
